TASK: Audit, Fix and Simplify Android UVC Camera Integration for Kiosk
1. Project context

I am developing an Android Kiosk application using Android Studio.

The final application will eventually support:

Face capture and face recognition.
Identity verification.
Displaying user information and academic scores after successful verification.

The kiosk hardware uses two USB UVC cameras:

Thermal camera — typically produces monochrome or thermal-related image data.
RGB camera — expected to provide normal color images.
Current development stage

The current milestone is ONLY camera integration and validation.

The application can already open and display an image from what I believe is the thermal camera. However, I have not confirmed whether the RGB camera is being detected, opened, and read correctly.

I want to simplify the current codebase and UI so that I can focus on establishing a reliable connection to both cameras.

2. Primary objectives

Work directly with the existing Android Studio project.

Your objectives are:

Understand the current application architecture before modifying anything.
Identify the exact UVC camera integration library and API currently used.
Verify how USB devices are discovered, how permission is requested, and how camera streams are initialized.
Determine whether both physical cameras can be opened and read independently.
Diagnose why the RGB camera may not be working or may be displaying monochrome images.
Remove or disable functionality that is unrelated to the current camera integration milestone.
Retain a small, reliable camera testing interface.
Build and test the application where the available environment permits.

Do not rebuild the application from scratch. Reuse the existing architecture and dependencies wherever practical.

